UnitRelayGovernance
├── when a deposit is admitted
│   └── it should checkpoint the principal and self-delegate the depositor
├── when holders express nominal votes
│   └── it should size each cast to the snapshot slice and book the consumption
├── when a vote is expressed
│   └── it should emit the preference from the relay address
├── when the ui prices a slice
│   └── it should answer the total and remaining budget without reverting
├── when the library views are called directly
│   └── it should price the same slice at the library address
├── when the yield token is sold
│   └── it should move no governance weight to the buyer
├── when buying the principal token
│   └── it should revert on every holder transfer path
├── when a holder withdraws
│   └── it should zero the checkpointed weight with the burned pair
├── given a freshly initialized relay
│   └── it should accept an express vote with nothing to attach
├── given the consumption ledger is read
│   └── it should keep the spent weight in relay storage
├── when a caller holds no snapshot principal
│   └── it should revert with NoVotingPower
├── when expressing a fractional split
│   └── it should forward the split untouched and consume its sum
├── when the fractional payload is malformed
│   └── it should revert with InvalidSupport
├── when the slice passes the component width
│   └── it should cap the cast at uint128 max and book the same amount
├── when a deposit is still pending at the snapshot
│   └── it should divide the queued weight among the holders already in
├── when a fractional split spends the whole slice
│   └── it should accept a split that sums to exactly the remaining budget
├── when the snapshot predates the relay
│   └── it should price a zero slice instead of reverting
├── when a holder delegated elsewhere receives more principal
│   └── it should keep the chosen delegate across the new mint
├── when the governor is rotated
│   ├── it should gate the rotation to the admin
│   ├── it should reject a zero governor
│   ├── it should reject a zero adapter
│   └── it should store the pair and emit the event
├── when a rotated governor reuses a proposal id
│   ├── it should let the holder spend a fresh slice on the colliding proposal
│   ├── it should book the fresh spend under the new governor
│   └── it should leave the old governor ledger untouched
├── when the adapter encodes a mint call
│   ├── it should refuse to send calldata whose selector is not the fractional cast
│   ├── it should mint no unbacked principal
│   └── it should leave the pair and the backing counter as they were
├── when the adapter encodes an arbitrary external call
│   ├── it should never reach the escrow with the transfer
│   └── it should refuse to send calldata whose selector is not the fractional cast
├── when the rotated pair encodes the fractional cast
│   ├── it should forward the fractional cast to the rotated governor
│   └── it should book the spent slice
├── when the proposal id fills the selector word
│   ├── it should forward the cast whatever the argument bytes share the selector word
│   └── it should book the spend
├── when the adapter returns calldata too short for a selector
│   └── it should refuse a payload that carries no selector at all
└── when the governor reverts the cast
    └── it should rebubble the governor revert verbatim
